{"id":"eli","name":"Eli","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:eli"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Eli","text":"Ascent, the high priest when the ark was at Shiloh (1 Sam. 1:3, 9). He was the first of the line of Ithamar, Aaron’s fourth son (1 Chr. 24:3; comp. 2 Sam. 8:17), who held that office. The office remained in his family till the time of Abiathar (1 Kings 2:26, 27), whom Solomon deposed, and appointed Zadok, of the family of Eleazar, in his stead (35). He acted also as a civil judge in Israel after the death of Samson (1 Sam. 4:18), and judged Israel for forty years. His sons Hophni and Phinehas grossly misconducted themselves, to the great disgust of the people (1 Sam. 2:27-36). They were licentious reprobates. He failed to reprove them so sternly as he ought to have done, and so brought upon his house the judgment of God (2:22-33; 3:18). The Israelites proclaimed war against the Philistines, whose army was encamped at Aphek. The battle, fought a short way beyond Mizpeh, ended in the …"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H5941","lemma":"עֵלִי","xlit":"ʻÊlîy","gloss":"Eli, an Israelite highpriest","kjv":"Eli","count":15,"share":0.39},{"strong":"H2652","lemma":"חׇפְנִי","xlit":"Chophnîy","gloss":"Chophni, an Israelite","kjv":"Hophni","count":3,"share":0.08},{"strong":"H7596","lemma":"שְׁאֵלָה","xlit":"shᵉʼêlâh","gloss":"a petition","kjv":"loan, petition, request","count":3,"share":0.08},{"strong":"H6372","lemma":"פִּינְחָס","xlit":"Pîynᵉchâç","gloss":"Pinechas, the name of three Israelites","kjv":"Phinehas","count":3,"share":0.08},{"strong":"H7592","lemma":"שָׁאַל","xlit":"shâʼal","gloss":"to inquire","kjv":"ask, beg, borrow, lay to charge","count":4,"share":0.11},{"strong":"H727","lemma":"אָרוֹן","xlit":"ʼârôwn","gloss":"a box","kjv":"ark, chest, coffin","count":4,"share":0.11}],"verses":["1Sam.1.14","1Sam.1.17","1Sam.1.25","1Sam.2.11","1Sam.2.20","1Sam.2.22","1Sam.2.27","1Sam.3.12","1Sam.3.14","1Sam.4.11","1Sam.4.13","1Sam.4.14","